# AGENTS.md: global repository rules

Canonical rules for every AI agent working in this repository. `CLAUDE.md` is a thin pointer to this file; Cursor, Codex, and OpenCode read this file natively. Edit rules here, once.

This repository uses a spec-driven work-tracking workflow. Strategy lives in [`ROADMAP.md`](ROADMAP.md); atomic work lives in [`.tasks/`](.tasks/); completed work is logged in [`CHANGELOG.md`](CHANGELOG.md).

---

## 0. Agent reading protocol (read this first)

To keep context windows small and relevant, an agent assigned a task reads exactly:

1. **This file** (`AGENTS.md`) in full: the global rules below.
2. **Its one assigned task file** in `.tasks/<id>.md`.
3. **Only the files that task names** in its `touched_files` frontmatter, plus any file the task body explicitly points to.

Do **not** scan the whole `.tasks/` directory, read other agents' task files, or read `ROADMAP.md`/`CHANGELOG.md` unless your task cites them. If your task's `depends_on` lists another task that is not yet in `.tasks/done/`, stop and report the blocker rather than doing its work.

## 1. Work altitude model (Epic -> Feature -> Task)

| Altitude | Tier | Lives in | Audience |
|---|---|---|---|
| 30,000 ft | Epic | `ROADMAP.md` phase/theme sections | human, planning |
| 10,000 ft | Feature | `ROADMAP.md` numbered forward-plan items | human, prioritizing |
| 1,000 ft | Task | `.tasks/<id>.md` | the assigned agent |
| 100 ft | acceptance | the task file's mechanical criteria | the agent, self-verifying |

A task file is the 1,000-foot decomposition of one roadmap Feature. Its `parent:` field links back up so an agent can trace intent without reading the roadmap. When a Feature is ready to build, it is decomposed into one or more task files; when every child task is done, the roadmap Feature is struck through.

